    "insights": [
      "The typography system relies entirely on Graphik for core UI, giving the interface a clean, modern, and highly legible geometric look.",
      "Extensive use of negative letter-spacing (tracking) across both headings (up to -0.04em) and body (-0.03em) creates a tightly locked, crisp, and slightly technical aesthetic.",
      "The semantic '.typo-' class structure (e.g., '.typo-display', '.typo-body-l') cleanly abstracts sizes and handles responsive scaling, stepping up sizes seamlessly at the 48rem breakpoint.",
      "PP Editorial New is present in the font definitions, suggesting a planned secondary serif typeface for brand or editorial moments, though Graphik handles all primary communication."
